# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# See docs/repository-layout.md for the canonical tree and the reasoning.
# The short version: provisioned bytes are never committed, sources always are.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- offline staging payload -----------------------------------------------
# Everything under deps/ is produced by provision_deps_*.sh / download_deps.sh
# and is far too large for git: the CANN toolkit alone is 1.2 GB, and the
# 950PR payload is 3.8 GB across the toolkit, NNAL, cann_extra, the local apt
# archive and a cp310 wheelhouse. It is declared by docker/<target>/deps.manifest
# and re-provisioned on demand, so nothing here is lost by not tracking it.
deps/

# Loose artefacts if a download script was pointed at the repository root.
*.run
*.whl
*.tar

# --- final deployable archives ---------------------------------------------
# artifacts/ holds exported images (docker save | pigz) and wheelhouse bundles
# on the Windows workspace filesystem. Multi-GB and regenerated on demand, so
# it is ignored twice over: by directory and by extension.
artifacts/
*.tar.gz

# --- build output from plugin source trees ---------------------------------
# csrc/ and src/ carry sources only. setup.py writes _version.py, _build_info.py,
# build/, .deps/ and compiled extensions back into the tree it builds, which is
# exactly why the Dockerfiles copy the checkout out of its read-only bind mount
# first. None of that belongs in git.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.deps/
*.so
*.o
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- local scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
*.log
